content='Below is a cleaned‑up version that:\n\n* keeps the original “Generate public SSH key” step but no longer redirects inside the command (the command just emits the key to stdout);\n* writes the key to a file with **ansible.builtin.copy** – the destination is quoted correctly and `force: no` guarantees the file is never overwritten;\n* guards all actions with explicit checks so missing variables (`user`, `user.ssh_key_directory`, `user.name`) won’t cause a playbook failure.\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Generate public SSH key for user\n  hosts: all\n  tasks:\n    # 1. Produce the public key on stdout\n    - name: Generate public SSH key (stdout)\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: ssh-keygen -y -f "{{ user.ssh_key_directory }}/{{ user.name }}"\n      register: pubkey_output\n      changed_when: False\n      args:\n        creates: "{{ user.ssh_key_directory }}/{{ user.name }}.pub"\n      when:\n        - user is defined\n        - user.ssh_key_directory is defined\n        - user.name is defined\n\n    # 2. Persist the key to a file, but only if it didn\'t already exist\n    - name: Write public SSH key to file\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        dest: "{{ user.ssh_key_directory }}/{{ user.name }}.pub"\n        content: "{{ pubkey_output.stdout }}"\n        force: no\n        mode: "0644"\n      when: pubkey_output is defined\n```\n\n* The first task runs `ssh-keygen` only when the destination `.pub` file does **not** already exist (`creates:`).  \n* The second task copies the captured stdout into that file, leaving an existing file untouched (`force: no`).  \n* All variable references are guarded (`when:` clauses) so that missing data does not abort the play.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'gpt-oss:20b', 'created_at': '2025-10-07T16:21:14.391550813Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 208059222379, 'load_duration': 164705249, 'prompt_eval_count': 2220, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1634850834, 'eval_count': 19404, 'ev